      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.55,
          "end": 5.1,
          "en": "-: Whoa! We already covered quite some things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.1,
          "end": 8.01,
          "en": "We learned how to add routes and how to load them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.01,
          "end": 11.61,
          "en": "either by typing it manually into our navigation bar here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.61,
          "end": 12.93,
          "en": "or by clicking some links.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.93,
          "end": 16.26,
          "en": "We also learned how to stall these links.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.26,
          "end": 18.21,
          "en": "But, what now, if we wanted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.21,
          "end": 20.37,
          "en": "to load a route programmatically?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.37,
          "end": 22.65,
          "en": "So we don't have a link, the user can click,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.65,
          "end": 25.02,
          "en": "but we finished some operation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.02,
          "end": 26.88,
          "en": "or the user clicked some button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.88,
          "end": 29.79,
          "en": "and then we want to trigger the navigation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.79,
          "end": 31.623,
          "en": "from our types good code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.785,
          "end": 33.618,
          "en": "We can do this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.618,
          "end": 35.64,
          "en": "Let's say, in our home component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 35.64,
          "end": 37.68,
          "en": "I add a new button to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 37.68,
          "end": 42.09,
          "en": "And, on this button, I simply want to load the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.09,
          "end": 43.71,
          "en": "the service page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 43.71,
          "end": 46.26,
          "en": "So here, now we could try adding router link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 46.26,
          "end": 49.5,
          "en": "but let's say I want to have a click listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 49.5,
          "end": 52.14,
          "en": "and execute some method because we do something else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 52.14,
          "end": 54.03,
          "en": "than just navigating there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 54.03,
          "end": 55.65,
          "en": "I will also add some CSS classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 55.65,
          "end": 57.84,
          "en": "to make this button look nice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 57.84,
          "end": 61.923,
          "en": "So, on this Click Listener, I want to execute onLoadServers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 62.983,
          "end": 66.78,
          "en": "And here this method now gets implemented",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 66.78,
          "end": 70.92,
          "en": "in the home component and onLoadServers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 70.92,
          "end": 73.47,
          "en": "I now still, again, I simply want to navigate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 73.47,
          "end": 74.82,
          "en": "to the service component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 74.82,
          "end": 76.74,
          "en": "So we could, for this example, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 76.74,
          "end": 79.35,
          "en": "always the user router link, but let's say here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 79.35,
          "end": 83.1,
          "en": "we have some complex calculation, or we reach out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 83.1,
          "end": 85.83,
          "en": "to our back, and we store something on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 85.83,
          "end": 90.21000000000001,
          "en": "And, once we are done, now we want to navigate away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 90.21000000000001,
          "end": 94.41,
          "en": "To do so, we somehow need to get access to our router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 94.41,
          "end": 96.907,
          "en": "this angular router, because we need to tell it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 96.907,
          "end": 99.39,
          "en": "\"Hey, please navigate somewhere else.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 99.39,
          "end": 102.36,
          "en": "The nice thing is we can check this router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 102.36,
          "end": 104.85,
          "en": "So let's bind it to a private property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 104.85,
          "end": 106.413,
          "en": "Maybe we name it router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 107.25,
          "end": 109.62,
          "en": "And this will be of type router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 109.62,
          "end": 113.72999999999999,
          "en": "Router needs to be imported from @angular/router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 113.72999999999999,
          "end": 116.67,
          "en": "With this injected, we can use this router here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 116.67,
          "end": 120.18,
          "en": "So this router, and then we get a couple of methods there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 120.18,
          "end": 123.6,
          "en": "One of the most important ones being Navigate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 123.6,
          "end": 126.24,
          "en": "Now Navigate takes an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 126.24,
          "end": 129.81,
          "en": "which allows us to, guess what, navigate to a new route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 129.81,
          "end": 132.66,
          "en": "And here a route is to find as an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 132.66,
          "end": 136.74,
          "en": "of the single or the different elements of this new path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 136.74,
          "end": 138.75,
          "en": "So, just like here, an app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 138.75,
          "end": 141.78,
          "en": "where I always explained this alternative way of binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 141.78,
          "end": 145.35,
          "en": "routing, binding it to an array where you could have users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 145.35,
          "end": 147.42000000000002,
          "en": "for the user's part of your path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 147.42000000000002,
          "end": 149.73,
          "en": "and then another element for maybe something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 149.73,
          "end": 152.22,
          "en": "for the something part of your path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 152.22,
          "end": 154.56,
          "en": "Now, you always have to pass such an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 154.56,
          "end": 156.27,
          "en": "when using the Navigate method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 156.27,
          "end": 158.22,
          "en": "But, in here still, the first element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 158.22,
          "end": 161.22,
          "en": "is simply the first element or the first segment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 161.22,
          "end": 162.32999999999998,
          "en": "of your path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 162.32999999999998,
          "end": 165.44,
          "en": "So if, let's say, we want to go to slash service here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 165.44,
          "end": 168.15,
          "en": "we could add slash service here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 168.15,
          "end": 171.06,
          "en": "And, as before, this is now an absolute path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 171.06,
          "end": 174.3,
          "en": "You could have a relative one, but here you have to control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 174.3,
          "end": 176.57999999999998,
          "en": "to what this should be relative to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 176.57999999999998,
          "end": 178.17000000000002,
          "en": "And I will come back to this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 178.17000000000002,
          "end": 181.44,
          "en": "So for now let's make it an absolute path here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 181.44,
          "end": 186.44,
          "en": "And, once we did this, let's check our page here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 186.57,
          "end": 189.57,
          "en": "click this button, and we go to servers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 189.57,
          "end": 193.53,
          "en": "So this is now programmatically routing to a different page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 193.53,
          "end": 195.63,
          "en": "Still, it doesn't reload our page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 195.63,
          "end": 198.27,
          "en": "It does the same as if we clicked a router link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 198.27,
          "end": 200.61,
          "en": "But, with this router navigate method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 200.61,
          "end": 203.4,
          "en": "we are able to trigger this programmatically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 203.4,
          "end": 205.833,
          "en": "so trigger this in our code.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
